+# InferenceService Refactoring
+
+This directory contains the refactored inference code for FastSpeech2 TTS.
+
+## Overview
+
+The `InferenceService` provides a clean, typed interface for text-to-speech
+synthesis. It encapsulates the entire inference pipeline into a single service
+with clear separation of concerns.
+
+**Note**: As of the latest update, `synthesize.py` now uses **only** the
+`InferenceService` for both single and batch modes. The old synthesis pipeline
+has been completely removed.
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Type Definitions (`types.py`)
+
+The refactoring introduces strongly-typed dataclasses for all inputs and
+outputs:
+
+- **`LanguageSpecifier`**: Specifies language (ISO 639-3 code) and segmentation
+  format
+- **`PhonemeSegment`**: A text segment with its phonemes
+- **`PhonemizeResult`**: Result of text-to-phoneme conversion
+- **`DurationResult`**: Duration predictions for each phoneme
+- **`PredictResult`**: Complete prediction including pitch, energy, and mel
+  spectrogram
+- **`InferResult`**: Final result with generated audio and extracted pitch
+
+### InferenceService (`inference_service.py`)
+
+The main service class that provides four key methods:
+
+#### 1. `phonemize(lang, text)`
+
+Converts text to phonemes.
+
+```python
+lang = LanguageSpecifier(iso639_3="eng", segmentation_format="librispeech")
+result = service.phonemize(lang, "Hello world")
+# result.segments = [
+#   PhonemeSegment(text="Hello", phonemes=["HH", "AH0", "L", "OW1"]),
+#   PhonemeSegment(text=" ", phonemes=["sp"]),
+#   PhonemeSegment(text="world", phonemes=["W", "ER1", "L", "D"])
+# ]
+```
+
+#### 2. `predict_duration(lang, phonemize_result, **opts)`
+
+Predicts duration for each phoneme.
+
+```python
+duration_result = service.predict_duration(
+    lang, phonemize_result, 
+    duration_control=1.0  # Optional: control speaking speed
+)
+# duration_result.durations_2d = [[123, 456, 789, 234], [567], [891, 345, 678, 912]]
+```
+
+#### 3. `predict_pitch_and_energy(lang, phonemize_result, duration_result, **opts)`
+
+Predicts pitch, energy, and generates mel spectrogram.
+
+```python
+predict_result = service.predict_pitch_and_energy(
+    lang, phonemize_result, duration_result,
+    pitch_control=1.0,    # Optional: control pitch
+    energy_control=1.0,   # Optional: control energy
+    duration_control=1.0  # Optional: control speed
+)
+```
+
+#### 4. `infer_audio(lang, predict_result)`
+
+Generates audio from predictions.
+
+```python
+infer_result = service.infer_audio(lang, predict_result)
+# infer_result.wav contains the generated audio
+# infer_result.actual_pitch contains extracted pitch contour
+```
+
+### Adapters (`adapters.py`)
+
+Bridge functions that connect the new typed interfaces with the existing
+FastSpeech2 codebase. These handle:
+
+- Loading configurations
+- Converting between old and new data formats
+- Preparing model inputs
+- Extracting predictions from model outputs
+
+## Usage
+
+### Basic Example
+
+```python
+from refactoring import InferenceService, LanguageSpecifier
+
+# Create service with configuration
+inference_service = InferenceService(
+    configuration_map={
+        "eng": {
+            "restore_step": 900000,
+            "p": "config/LJSpeech/preprocess.yaml",
+            "m": "config/LJSpeech/model.yaml",
+            "t": "config/LJSpeech/train.yaml",
+        },
+        "cmn": {
+            "speaker_id": 1,
+            "restore_step": 600000,
+            "p": "config/AISHELL3/preprocess.yaml",
+            "m": "config/AISHELL3/model.yaml",
+            "t": "config/AISHELL3/train.yaml",
+        },
+    }
+)
+
+# Specify language
+lang = LanguageSpecifier(
+    iso639_3="cmn", 
+    segmentation_format="fastspeech2-pinyin-r"
+)
+
+# Run inference pipeline
+text = "你好，世界！"
+phonemize_result = inference_service.phonemize(lang, text)
+duration_result = inference_service.predict_duration(lang, phonemize_result)
+predict_result = inference_service.predict_pitch_and_energy(
+    lang, phonemize_result, duration_result,
+    pitch_control=1.0,
+    energy_control=1.0,
+    duration_control=1.0
+)
+infer_result = inference_service.infer_audio(lang, predict_result)
+
+# Save outputs using utility functions
+from utils.tools import (
+    save_infer_result_audio,
+    save_infer_result_visualization,
+    save_infer_result_prosody
+)
+
+save_infer_result_audio(infer_result, "output", "output/")
+save_infer_result_visualization(infer_result, "output", "output/", "stats.json")
+save_infer_result_prosody(infer_result, text, "output", "output/", "mandarin")
+```
+
+### Command Line Usage
+
+`synthesize.py` now uses InferenceService exclusively:
+
+```bash
+# English synthesis (single mode)
+uv run python synthesize.py \
+    --mode single \
+    --text "Hello world" \
+    --restore_step 900000 \
+    -p config/LJSpeech/preprocess.yaml \
+    -m config/LJSpeech/model.yaml \
+    -t config/LJSpeech/train.yaml
+
+# Mandarin synthesis (single mode)
+uv run python synthesize.py \
+    --mode single \
+    --text "你好，世界！" \
+    --speaker_id 1 \
+    --restore_step 600000 \
+    -p config/AISHELL3/preprocess.yaml \
+    -m config/AISHELL3/model.yaml \
+    -t config/AISHELL3/train.yaml
+
+# Batch synthesis
+uv run python synthesize.py \
+    --mode batch \
+    --source preprocessed_data/AISHELL3/val.txt \
+    --restore_step 600000 \
+    -p config/AISHELL3/preprocess.yaml \
+    -m config/AISHELL3/model.yaml \
+    -t config/AISHELL3/train.yaml
+
+# Copy prosody data to clipboard (single mode only)
+uv run python synthesize.py \
+    --mode single \
+    --text "你好，世界！" \
+    --speaker_id 1 \
+    --restore_step 600000 \
+    -p config/AISHELL3/preprocess.yaml \
+    -m config/AISHELL3/model.yaml \
+    -t config/AISHELL3/train.yaml \
+    --copy-prosody-data-only
+```
+
+## Helper Functions in `utils/tools.py`
+
+New helper functions have been added to work with the refactored types:
+
+- **`save_predict_result_visualization()`**: Save mel spectrogram without actual
+  pitch
+- **`save_infer_result_visualization()`**: Save mel spectrogram with actual
+  pitch overlay
+- **`save_infer_result_audio()`**: Save generated audio
+- **`save_infer_result_prosody()`**: Save prosody JSON
+- **`generate_prosody_json_from_infer_result()`**: Generate prosody data from
+  InferResult
+
+### Removed Functions
+
+The following functions have been removed from `utils/tools.py` as they are no
+longer needed:
+
+- **`synth_samples()`**: Replaced by the new helper functions above
+
+Functions still used by `train.py` and `evaluate.py` are kept:
+
+- `preprocess_english()`, `preprocess_mandarin()` (also used by adapters)
+- `to_device()`, `synth_one_sample()`
+
+## Benefits of the Refactoring
+
+1. **Type Safety**: All inputs and outputs are strongly typed using Python
+   dataclasses
+2. **Clear Separation**: Each step of the pipeline is a separate method with
+   clear inputs/outputs
+3. **Testability**: Each component can be tested independently
+4. **Flexibility**: Easy to swap implementations or add new features
+5. **Documentation**: Types serve as inline documentation
+6. **Reusability**: The service can be instantiated and reused across multiple
+   requests
+7. **Simplified Code**: Removed old synthesis pipeline, using only
+   InferenceService
+
+## Python Version
+
+This code requires Python 3.12+ for the modern type hinting syntax (e.g.,
+`list[str]`, `dict[str, Any]`).
